1
00:00:00,777 --> 00:00:09,157
I found myself lost and alone on this journey

2
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:17,497
Though my heart wandered far and wide, I could move not an inch

3
00:00:17,497 --> 00:00:22,587
But now I can depart for any distant land

4
00:00:22,587 --> 00:00:25,717
But now I can depart for any distant land

5
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,757
Now that we've met on this road

6
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:34,557
Now that we've met on this road

7
00:00:35,057 --> 00:00:42,397
Even the unfamiliar songs of travelers

8
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:53,157
Can spark nostalgia in me when I'm with you

9
00:00:53,157 --> 00:00:57,037
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

10
00:00:57,037 --> 00:01:01,417
If the world we dreamed of exists somewhere,

11
00:01:01,417 --> 00:01:09,847
Then let's go search for it beyond the wind

12
00:01:09,847 --> 00:01:13,807
Through chilling dawns,

13
00:01:13,807 --> 00:01:18,227
Through arid noons,

14
00:01:18,227 --> 00:01:22,187
Through shivering nights,

15
00:01:22,187 --> 00:01:28,197
Let's go see what lies at the end

16
00:01:58,587 --> 00:02:03,347
Yeah, there was quite a bit of talk about it on the way here from Lubinheigen.

17
00:02:03,347 --> 00:02:05,267
Yep, how creepy!

18
00:02:05,267 --> 00:02:08,817
Are you talking about the sorcerer who appeared on the new road?

19
00:02:08,817 --> 00:02:10,617
I heard about that.

20
00:02:11,777 --> 00:02:14,537
They say it can summon wolves to be its puppets.

21
00:02:14,537 --> 00:02:18,497
They attack travelers in order to consume their blood.

22
00:02:18,497 --> 00:02:19,497
No way.

23
00:02:21,417 --> 00:02:24,667
It's no joke. You better be careful.

24
00:02:24,667 --> 00:02:28,167
In Lubinheigen, I heard the rumors from a member of the Church.

25
00:02:28,167 --> 00:02:32,427
An entire caravan was attacked two weeks ago.

26
00:02:32,427 --> 00:02:35,597
Whoa, creepy... Really creepy, isn't it?

27
00:02:36,217 --> 00:02:38,387
I'm gonna drown this fear with more booze.

28
00:02:39,097 --> 00:02:41,147
Couldn't hurt for me to take note.

29
00:02:42,307 --> 00:02:45,727
I pray, for your sake, that the sorcerer isn't a woman.

30
00:02:46,847 --> 00:02:47,897
Why's that?

31
00:02:47,897 --> 00:02:50,487
You're easily fooled by women,

32
00:02:50,487 --> 00:02:52,607
and slow to recover when you get hurt.

33
00:02:54,737 --> 00:02:57,857
You've been drinking more heavily ever since that day.

34
00:03:00,287 --> 00:03:01,577
H-Hey...

35
00:03:02,707 --> 00:03:05,447
It's the talk of nearly every tavern we visit,

36
00:03:05,957 --> 00:03:07,797
the Medio Trading deal.

37
00:03:11,087 --> 00:03:14,427
Men really are dumb creatures.

38
00:03:14,427 --> 00:03:16,757
Well, excuse me for being dumb.

39
00:03:16,757 --> 00:03:21,767
Wolf and a Proper Balance

40
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:24,397
What an inconsiderate town this is!

41
00:03:24,397 --> 00:03:26,317
They close the tavern far too early!

42
00:03:26,317 --> 00:03:29,777
This place is a satellite of the Church stronghold Lubinheigen, after all.

43
00:03:29,777 --> 00:03:32,267
Be thankful they let someone run a tavern for travelers at all.

44
00:03:32,817 --> 00:03:37,437
So this town's only interested in living a humble life and offering prayers to God?

45
00:03:38,067 --> 00:03:43,877
It's best known for the citizens putting you to sleep with talk about how profound the latest sermon was.

46
00:03:44,707 --> 00:03:47,447
Hard to believe anyone could enjoy a life like that.

47
00:03:47,877 --> 00:03:52,577
We'll head to Lubinheigen once I sell the pepper and purchase new goods.

48
00:03:53,087 --> 00:03:54,757
Is it a large town?

49
00:03:54,757 --> 00:03:57,347
Yeah, bigger than Pazzio.

50
00:03:57,347 --> 00:03:59,057
It's a city rather than a town.

51
00:03:59,057 --> 00:04:01,677
It's a busy place with lots of street stalls.

52
00:04:01,677 --> 00:04:02,967
Will there be any apples?

53
00:04:03,387 --> 00:04:05,307
I'm not sure about raw apples.

54
00:04:05,307 --> 00:04:07,847
This is the season for preserves.

55
00:04:08,937 --> 00:04:09,847
Preserves?

56
00:04:10,437 --> 00:04:12,147
I'm not talking about pickled goods.

57
00:04:12,147 --> 00:04:13,357
Fruits preserved in honey.

58
00:04:14,357 --> 00:04:15,567
Oh?

59
00:04:15,567 --> 00:04:16,987
Not just apples, either.

60
00:04:16,987 --> 00:04:19,197
Pears preserved in honey taste good, too.

61
00:04:19,197 --> 00:04:21,617
And they started doing peaches recently.

62
00:04:22,197 --> 00:04:23,567
Peaches...

63
00:04:24,327 --> 00:04:27,877
Thinly sliced peaches are stacked inside a barrel.

64
00:04:27,877 --> 00:04:31,797
The best products even have figs and almonds inside.

65
00:04:31,797 --> 00:04:34,447
Ginger is added after honey is poured on the peaches.

66
00:04:34,447 --> 00:04:38,007
They stew for two months like that.

67
00:04:40,557 --> 00:04:45,307
The sweet sensation that fills your mouth is unlike anything in this world.

68
00:04:45,307 --> 00:04:48,717
It's not surprising that the Church was considering banning the stuff.

69
00:04:49,437 --> 00:04:51,937
Hey, you're drooling.

70
00:04:54,447 --> 00:04:57,157
You're not toying with me, are you?

71
00:04:57,157 --> 00:05:01,157
I'm not, but peach preserves are a product of the wealthy.

72
00:05:01,157 --> 00:05:03,107
You don't really find them just up for sale.

73
00:05:03,537 --> 00:05:07,117
But what if we do? Could we buy them if we do?

74
00:05:07,117 --> 00:05:09,957
O-Okay, I'll buy some for you.

75
00:05:09,957 --> 00:05:10,917
You have to!

76
00:05:11,457 --> 00:05:12,877
Only a little, though.

77
00:05:13,337 --> 00:05:15,417
That's a promise, okay?

78
00:05:15,417 --> 00:05:17,587
H-Hey, are you listening to me?

79
00:05:17,587 --> 00:05:18,547
Let's go.

80
00:05:19,637 --> 00:05:21,257
Let's go right now.

81
00:05:21,257 --> 00:05:22,767
Go where?

82
00:05:22,767 --> 00:05:26,977
Where else? We'll go to the inn, get our cart, and go to Whatever Trading Company.

83
00:05:26,977 --> 00:05:31,227
We're going to wake the person there, get good money for our pepper, and head to Lubinheigen.

84
00:05:31,477 --> 00:05:33,937
Wait a second. At this hour of the night?

85
00:05:33,937 --> 00:05:35,227
It might sell out soon.

86
00:05:35,567 --> 00:05:37,147
That would be a total catastrophe.

87
00:05:37,817 --> 00:05:41,227
The market probably won't have them on sale in the first place, let alone sell out!

88
00:05:41,237 --> 00:05:44,397
Peaches and honey... That's hard to believe.

89
00:05:44,397 --> 00:05:45,947
Mind-boggling, even.

90
00:05:45,947 --> 00:05:47,697
Don't treat this like a sure thing.

91
00:05:49,707 --> 00:05:50,747
However...

92
00:05:51,787 --> 00:05:53,457
It's hard to give up pears.

93
00:05:55,957 --> 00:06:01,967
The pastor's sermons moved our hearts quite a bit.

94
00:06:01,967 --> 00:06:06,137
It was literally a blessing from God.

95
00:06:06,137 --> 00:06:13,147
His words gave us motivation to strive for greater service to the Lord.

96
00:06:14,057 --> 00:06:18,067
Well, I rambled on a bit there, but shall we start discussing our business?

97
00:06:18,067 --> 00:06:19,567
Yes, let's.

98
00:06:20,107 --> 00:06:22,947
What do you have to offer today?

99
00:06:23,577 --> 00:06:24,907
This is it.

100
00:06:24,907 --> 00:06:26,947
Pepper, is it?

101
00:06:27,617 --> 00:06:29,027
You know your goods.

102
00:06:29,037 --> 00:06:31,157
It's the scent.

103
00:06:36,257 --> 00:06:37,547
Impressive.

104
00:06:37,547 --> 00:06:41,247
Not at all. It's just a matter of experience.

105
00:06:41,657 --> 00:06:46,177
You wouldn't happen to have your own scale, would you?

106
00:06:50,097 --> 00:06:54,817
I don't have one, but I have faith in God.

107
00:06:59,647 --> 00:07:01,737
In any case, what bad luck for me.

108
00:07:01,737 --> 00:07:05,167
The demand for pepper has increased significantly as of late.

109
00:07:05,167 --> 00:07:07,827
If you had come a week earlier,

110
00:07:07,827 --> 00:07:10,817
I could have taken it off your hands for nothing at all!

111
00:07:11,457 --> 00:07:13,627
Sounds like I came in at just the right time.

112
00:07:13,627 --> 00:07:17,957
Indeed. Let's proceed with the weighing of the pepper.

113
00:07:18,297 --> 00:07:20,007
Yes, please.

114
00:07:20,547 --> 00:07:24,717
Let's see, we'll need paper and ink.
Wait just a moment, please.

115
00:07:30,517 --> 00:07:31,247
What is it?

116
00:07:31,847 --> 00:07:33,477
I'm thirsty.

117
00:07:34,187 --> 00:07:35,357
You'll have to wait.

118
00:07:43,527 --> 00:07:45,777
Will water be okay?

119
00:07:45,777 --> 00:07:47,647
I have some wine as well.

120
00:07:48,077 --> 00:07:50,447
Oh, water, if you please.

121
00:07:50,447 --> 00:07:52,247
Not a problem.

122
00:07:59,667 --> 00:08:02,677
That's forty-five measures' worth, then.

123
00:08:02,677 --> 00:08:04,717
Where does this pepper come from?

124
00:08:04,717 --> 00:08:07,257
Ramapata, in the Kingdom of Leedon.

125
00:08:07,257 --> 00:08:09,427
Milone Trading conducted the import.

126
00:08:11,427 --> 00:08:16,227
Ramapata is famous for its spices,

127
00:08:16,227 --> 00:08:19,357
and the certificate looks to be genuine.

128
00:08:19,897 --> 00:08:25,897
How does one Lumione gold coin per measure sound to you?

129
00:08:26,317 --> 00:08:29,787
What's the exchange rate for Lumione gold coins?

130
00:08:29,787 --> 00:08:33,327
Do you want the value in Trenni silver coins?

131
00:08:33,327 --> 00:08:34,157
Yes.

132
00:08:34,157 --> 00:08:39,707
Thirty-two and five-sixths Trenni silver coins.

133
00:08:39,707 --> 00:08:41,297
That's the current exchange rate.

134
00:08:49,677 --> 00:08:51,177
I accept the offer.

135
00:08:51,177 --> 00:08:53,057
Oh, in that case...

136
00:08:56,397 --> 00:08:57,727
Is something wrong?

137
00:08:58,807 --> 00:09:00,137
I feel dizzy...

138
00:09:00,147 --> 00:09:02,647
A-Are you all right?

139
00:09:03,027 --> 00:09:04,607
Y-Yes...

140
00:09:06,277 --> 00:09:07,987
Do you feel better?

141
00:09:08,407 --> 00:09:10,947
Yes, thank you.

142
00:09:10,947 --> 00:09:13,497
A long journey will tire even a strong man.

143
00:09:13,497 --> 00:09:15,737
I'll bring some goat milk for you.

144
00:09:16,207 --> 00:09:17,667
Sir?

145
00:09:18,747 --> 00:09:24,337
These scales still seem tilted to my eyes.

146
00:09:24,627 --> 00:09:27,927
Do they look that way to you?

147
00:09:29,047 --> 00:09:31,637
No, that certainly couldn't be the case.

148
00:09:31,637 --> 00:09:34,427
I know it couldn't, but...

149
00:09:34,427 --> 00:09:35,927
Whoa!

150
00:09:37,137 --> 00:09:38,647
Hey, are you all right?

151
00:09:39,937 --> 00:09:42,517
My eyes don't seem to be working correctly.

152
00:09:49,197 --> 00:09:53,647
It seems that what I drank was wine, not water.

153
00:09:54,367 --> 00:09:56,657
Isn't that right, sir?

154
00:10:00,377 --> 00:10:05,007
As the proverb says, "The rowdier the pub, the more sober its master."

155
00:10:05,007 --> 00:10:05,667
I see now.

156
00:10:06,667 --> 00:10:11,097
The secret to success is being the only sober one, eh?

157
00:10:12,347 --> 00:10:14,557
It seems I'm drunk on the same wine as my companion.

158
00:10:14,557 --> 00:10:18,267
I doubt we'll remember some of the things we've seen and heard here.

159
00:10:18,267 --> 00:10:22,397
However, drunkards have been known to demand unreasonable things.

160
00:10:22,397 --> 00:10:23,557
W-What do youâ€”

161
00:10:24,267 --> 00:10:29,947
You'll pay the initial sum you offered, the amount you were to profit from this deal, and, let's see...

162
00:10:29,947 --> 00:10:33,187
You'll allow me to buy double all that on loan.

163
00:10:33,197 --> 00:10:36,107
Double? That's out of the question.

164
00:10:36,657 --> 00:10:38,997
Oh, that's too bad.

165
00:10:38,997 --> 00:10:40,747
Feels like the wine is wearing off.

166
00:10:42,667 --> 00:10:44,797
Let's talk about the merchandise.

167
00:10:44,797 --> 00:10:48,797
Given the large sum involved here, why don't you pay me in high quality weapons and armor?

168
00:10:48,797 --> 00:10:50,757
Arms, you say?

169
00:10:53,007 --> 00:10:56,717
They're always a good bet for turning a safe profit.

170
00:10:56,717 --> 00:10:59,517
I can get the loan back to you quickly that way.

171
00:10:59,517 --> 00:11:02,507
I imagine you've got arms bound for Lubinheigen, don't you?

172
00:11:02,937 --> 00:11:05,147
Arms, you say...

173
00:11:05,647 --> 00:11:09,397
You must have connections to other trading companies in Lubinheigen, right?

174
00:11:09,397 --> 00:11:12,657
Selling them there will balance out the books.

175
00:11:13,737 --> 00:11:15,777
What say you?

176
00:11:17,907 --> 00:11:19,577
Thank you very much.

177
00:11:19,577 --> 00:11:22,827
Could you arrange for the goods immediately?

178
00:11:22,827 --> 00:11:25,497
I hope to leave for Lubinheigen as soon as possible.

179
00:11:25,497 --> 00:11:27,207
V-Very well.

180
00:11:27,207 --> 00:11:28,707
What about the appraisal?

181
00:11:29,207 --> 00:11:33,427
I'll leave that to you. After all, I have faith in God.

182
00:11:44,897 --> 00:11:46,147
Poor man.

183
00:11:46,147 --> 00:11:49,147
I'm surprised you noticed.

184
00:11:49,647 --> 00:11:53,107
I'm beautiful, I'm wise, and my tail's fur is sleek.

185
00:11:53,107 --> 00:11:55,067
But my eyes and ears are also keen.

186
00:11:55,067 --> 00:11:57,657
I noticed as soon as I set foot inside this place.

187
00:11:58,327 --> 00:11:59,157
Did you?

188
00:11:59,157 --> 00:12:00,657
What's that supposed to mean?

189
00:12:01,457 --> 00:12:03,247
What's gotten into you?

190
00:12:03,827 --> 00:12:07,827
Experience may lead to self-confidence, but pride goes before a fall.

191
00:12:08,587 --> 00:12:10,327
Didn't Chloe teach you that?

192
00:12:11,877 --> 00:12:13,087
You're absolutely right.

193
00:12:13,087 --> 00:12:14,247
You fool!

194
00:12:15,217 --> 00:12:16,707
Don't go sulking about it!

195
00:12:17,547 --> 00:12:19,467
Learn from the experience and move on.

196
00:12:31,027 --> 00:12:31,987
Oil?

197
00:12:31,987 --> 00:12:35,607
Yes, I hear it's good for grooming my tail.

198
00:12:36,027 --> 00:12:38,487
Can you buy some for me when we reach the next town?

199
00:12:41,827 --> 00:12:45,667
The clothes you're wearing now, your change of clothes, your comb,

200
00:12:45,667 --> 00:12:50,877
your traveling expenses, food, and the <i>huge</i> amount of wine... have you bothered to add all that up?

201
00:12:51,507 --> 00:12:54,337
There's the head tax I have to pay every time we enter a town, as well.

202
00:12:54,337 --> 00:12:57,587
Surely you're not telling me you can't do sums.

203
00:12:57,587 --> 00:13:00,217
I can do addition.

204
00:13:00,217 --> 00:13:02,717
I'm good at subtraction, too.

205
00:13:02,727 --> 00:13:06,347
In that case, add up what you've used.

206
00:13:06,347 --> 00:13:09,687
If you're such a wise wolf, you should be able to work out my answer from that.

207
00:13:10,577 --> 00:13:12,527
Indeed I can.

208
00:13:14,897 --> 00:13:16,727
You'll buy me some for sure.

209
00:13:17,237 --> 00:13:21,327
Just look what happens to the wits of the proud wise wolf when she has too much wine.

210
00:13:21,327 --> 00:13:24,867
I'm not drunk, you know.

211
00:13:24,867 --> 00:13:26,867
Idiot! What are you...

212
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:28,377
Just kidding.

213
00:13:29,457 --> 00:13:30,707
Geez...

214
00:13:31,127 --> 00:13:34,757
You shouldn't underestimate me.

215
00:13:34,757 --> 00:13:42,467
Surely you don't think I missed how much you gained
from taking advantage of that appraiser's weakness?

216
00:13:43,097 --> 00:13:45,467
Will you buy me some oil?

217
00:13:45,797 --> 00:13:49,557
Do you know how much money you still owe me?

218
00:13:49,557 --> 00:13:51,517
A hundred and forty silver coins.

219
00:13:51,517 --> 00:13:53,937
I'm sure you realize that's a small fortune.

220
00:13:54,527 --> 00:13:56,817
How do you expect me to spend even more on luxuries?

221
00:13:57,987 --> 00:14:01,817
What? You want me to repay my debt that badly?

222
00:14:02,157 --> 00:14:04,327
Of. Course. I. Do.

223
00:14:06,787 --> 00:14:09,577
So that's how you've been thinking.

224
00:14:10,417 --> 00:14:11,417
What do you mean?

225
00:14:11,417 --> 00:14:17,717
Well, I suppose if I pay my debts, that makes me a free wolf.

226
00:14:17,717 --> 00:14:22,097
Oh, well. I suppose I should pay you back as soon as possible and head back north myself.

227
00:14:22,427 --> 00:14:25,467
I'm accustomed to solitude, anyway.

228
00:14:30,937 --> 00:14:33,727
We didn't decide the due date for payment.

229
00:14:33,727 --> 00:14:36,927
It'll be fine so long as I get it before we reach the northern woods.

230
00:14:37,897 --> 00:14:39,237
Will that do?

231
00:14:39,237 --> 00:14:45,197
Yes, I should think I'll be able to repay you by the time we reach the north country.

232
00:14:48,997 --> 00:14:54,007
And it's my intention to pay you back with interest.

233
00:14:54,007 --> 00:14:59,607
In other words, the more I borrow, the greater profit for you. You see?

234
00:15:01,887 --> 00:15:03,337
Oil, huh?

235
00:15:03,337 --> 00:15:07,837
Yes. You can put it on my tab,
so could you buy some for me?

236
00:15:13,687 --> 00:15:15,357
It's a deal.

237
00:15:15,357 --> 00:15:16,477
Thank you.

238
00:15:29,077 --> 00:15:32,247
What a beautiful day for grooming.

239
00:15:42,047 --> 00:15:46,927
By the way, you got quite the discount on those goods, didn't you?

240
00:15:46,927 --> 00:15:48,677
Why do you want to know?

241
00:15:50,427 --> 00:15:54,437
Well, I wouldn't want to sponge off a traveling merchant who's barely scraping by.

242
00:15:54,437 --> 00:15:59,687
Arms sell fast in Lubinheigen, but there are many merchants who sell them.

243
00:16:00,107 --> 00:16:04,817
There isn't a lot of profit to be had,
so getting a lower price can only do so much.

244
00:16:04,817 --> 00:16:07,527
But since you bought this much, will you not make some profit?

245
00:16:09,907 --> 00:16:13,167
Well, it should cover the cost of some oil.

246
00:16:14,457 --> 00:16:15,827
That's good to hear.

247
00:16:17,497 --> 00:16:21,297
You know, in comparison to this load, spices are divine.

248
00:16:21,297 --> 00:16:22,927
Did you have a taste?

249
00:16:22,927 --> 00:16:24,677
I'm not like you, you glutton.

250
00:16:24,677 --> 00:16:25,747
I'm talking about profit.

251
00:16:26,967 --> 00:16:29,677
Why don't you trade spices again, then?

252
00:16:29,677 --> 00:16:32,807
Their prices in Lubinheigen aren't much higher than in Poroson.

253
00:16:32,807 --> 00:16:35,057
I'd take a loss from selling spices due to tariffs.

254
00:16:35,057 --> 00:16:37,057
Then give it up, I say.

255
00:16:38,437 --> 00:16:41,567
If I could sell other commodities at the same profit margin as spices,

256
00:16:41,567 --> 00:16:43,607
I'd be able to open a store in no time at all.

257
00:16:44,277 --> 00:16:45,947
Surely there's something.

258
00:16:45,947 --> 00:16:50,287
Jewels and gold seem like they'd sell well.

259
00:16:50,287 --> 00:16:54,157
Those kinds of items aren't too profitable in Lubinheigen.

260
00:16:55,287 --> 00:16:56,867
Why's that?

261
00:16:59,377 --> 00:17:01,377
The tariff is way too high.

262
00:17:01,377 --> 00:17:06,677
They levy serious taxes on all but a certain group of merchants.

263
00:17:06,677 --> 00:17:08,597
There's no business to be had there.

264
00:17:09,047 --> 00:17:12,597
Why are certain merchants exempt?

265
00:17:12,597 --> 00:17:15,807
They have ties with the Church.

266
00:17:15,807 --> 00:17:20,607
They bring gold bars to Lubinheigen, and those bars are inscribed with the Holy Seal.

267
00:17:20,607 --> 00:17:24,147
Once the gold becomes blessed that way, it fetches an absurdly high price.

268
00:17:24,527 --> 00:17:28,227
The Church receives generous donations in return.

269
00:17:28,567 --> 00:17:30,617
What a corrupt system.

270
00:17:31,037 --> 00:17:34,577
That's why they're extremely strict about smuggling.

271
00:17:37,037 --> 00:17:41,957
Smuggled gold would probably sell for twice the market price, but there are too many risks involved.

272
00:17:41,957 --> 00:17:44,867
There aren't any idiots dumb enough to take their chances.

273
00:17:45,547 --> 00:17:48,387
Could gold really be that hard to hide?

274
00:17:48,387 --> 00:17:51,087
Their cargo inspections are pretty thorough.

275
00:17:52,177 --> 00:17:54,137
What happens to those who are caught?

276
00:17:54,477 --> 00:17:57,137
They'll cut off your right hand, at the very least.

277
00:17:58,937 --> 00:18:00,977
It just isn't worth the risk.

278
00:18:03,147 --> 00:18:07,647
Well, your business is doing well enough. There's nothing wrong with making steady coin.

279
00:18:07,647 --> 00:18:13,577
I tend to agree, but a certain someone's spending all my hard-earned money.

280
00:18:27,717 --> 00:18:29,637
You better be careful along the way.

281
00:18:32,467 --> 00:18:35,097
It looks like mercenaries have arrived from the north.

282
00:18:35,097 --> 00:18:36,557
Mercenaries?

283
00:18:36,557 --> 00:18:37,097
Yeah.

284
00:18:38,137 --> 00:18:41,607
Traveling on this path would be suicide, then.

285
00:18:41,607 --> 00:18:45,857
Yeah, they spot their prey faster than a hawk on the wing

286
00:18:45,857 --> 00:18:49,317
and take everything of value, down to the leaves on the turnips.

287
00:18:50,107 --> 00:18:52,867
They're armed with long spears, too.

288
00:18:52,867 --> 00:18:55,607
Even I have stories to tell about the trouble they've caused.

289
00:18:56,077 --> 00:19:00,117
I was surprised to hear that they've come this far south.

290
00:19:00,117 --> 00:19:02,707
Same as us merchants, they only move based on profit and loss.

291
00:19:05,297 --> 00:19:08,127
Well, it's pointless to think about it here.

292
00:19:08,127 --> 00:19:12,047
In any case, let's head to Lubinheigen by using the new side road.

293
00:19:13,547 --> 00:19:16,637
You're not afraid of pagan sorcerers, are you?

294
00:19:16,637 --> 00:19:17,307
No.

295
00:19:17,977 --> 00:19:20,807
They say there are packs of wolves on the side route.

296
00:19:20,807 --> 00:19:22,517
They're easier to deal with than humans.

297
00:19:23,687 --> 00:19:25,937
At least I can reason with them.

298
00:19:25,937 --> 00:19:28,987
I'll leave the negotiations to you, then.

299
00:19:39,037 --> 00:19:41,537
There's no one in sight.

300
00:19:41,537 --> 00:19:44,037
Rumors of a thing usually hold more power than the thing itself.

301
00:19:47,417 --> 00:19:49,717
How boring. I'm going to take a nap.

302
00:19:50,507 --> 00:19:53,637
You'll notice wolves approaching even if you're asleep, right?

303
00:19:53,637 --> 00:19:56,057
Of course I will!

304
00:19:56,057 --> 00:19:58,017
It'll be a hassle if they surround us.

305
00:19:58,467 --> 00:20:00,267
You worry too much.

306
00:20:00,267 --> 00:20:04,097
Most animals are quite aware, be they sleeping or awake.

307
00:20:04,097 --> 00:20:07,017
It's only you humans who are defenseless in slumber.

308
00:20:07,017 --> 00:20:10,527
You'd be more convincing if you snored less.

309
00:20:10,527 --> 00:20:12,447
I don't snore!

310
00:20:12,777 --> 00:20:15,157
Well, it's not that loud, I suppose.

311
00:20:15,157 --> 00:20:16,987
I told you I don't snore!

312
00:20:16,987 --> 00:20:18,617
Okay, okay.

313
00:20:18,617 --> 00:20:20,407
I don't snore at all!

314
00:20:21,287 --> 00:20:23,077
I get the message.

315
00:20:26,247 --> 00:20:27,247
What is it?

316
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:30,797
I'll let you handle these negotiations.

317
00:20:34,587 --> 00:20:35,887
Who's ahead of us?

318
00:20:36,717 --> 00:20:39,007
The kind of human that I despise.

319
00:20:39,887 --> 00:20:41,677
Are you talking about the sorcerer?

320
00:21:01,787 --> 00:21:02,827
Sheep?

321
00:21:07,287 --> 00:21:09,287
Is that the sorcerer we've heard about?

322
00:21:22,977 --> 00:21:24,887
What was all that about?

323
00:21:24,887 --> 00:21:27,647
It's a ritual for when you meet a shepherd.

324
00:21:27,647 --> 00:21:30,857
At least we know he isn't a sorcerer.

325
00:21:31,727 --> 00:21:34,107
I'm Lawrence, a traveling merchant.

326
00:21:34,107 --> 00:21:36,107
This is my partner, Holo.

327
00:21:37,867 --> 00:21:43,237
I'd like to ask the shepherd I've met under God's guidance to offer prayers for our safety.

328
00:21:47,577 --> 00:21:48,827
With pleasure.

329
00:23:41,007 --> 00:23:44,397
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and the Shepherd's Lamb."</i>

330
00:23:45,877 --> 00:23:49,407
<i>Next Episode: "Wolf and the Shepherd's Lamb."</i>

